# Build artifacts from running the toolchain inside the checkout
# (R CMD INSTALL, R CMD build, R CMD check).
#
# Scope: the git working tree only. This file has no effect on the
# distribution tarball -- .Rbuildignore does that job.
#
# In particular, do NOT add the tracked `cleanup` script here. It is not
# redundant with this file: R CMD build runs it automatically (R-exts 1.2) to
# strip the generated src/Makevars out of the tarball, and `configure`
# regenerates src/Makevars from src/Makevars.in on every platform. Without it a
# developer's macOS -lgomp Makevars leaks into a Linux CRAN build.

# --- compiled objects and shared/static libraries ---
*.o
*.so
*.dll
*.a
*.dylib

# --- generated build configuration ---
# configure renders this from the tracked src/Makevars.in. The rule is
# deliberately narrow: src/Makevars.in and src/Makevars.win are tracked and
# must stay visible, so do not widen this to src/Makevars*.
/src/Makevars

# --- R CMD build / R CMD check output ---
*.tar.gz
*.Rcheck/
*.out

# --- coverage report written to the repo root by .github/workflows/test-coverage.yaml ---
/cobertura.xml

# --- pkgdown site, built into docs/ by .github/workflows/pkgdown.yaml ---
# (the tracked pkgdown/ directory holds the site config and is not ignored)
/docs/

# --- R session and editor/OS junk ---
.Rhistory
.RData
.Ruserdata
.Rproj.user/
.DS_Store

# --- defensive ---
# Not produced by the toolchain used here (verified absent after
# R CMD INSTALL on R 4.6.1), but src/symbols.rds is a real R install artifact
# and is cheap to keep out of history.
/src/symbols.rds
